        ]
      },
      "worked": "Fix one person to remove rotational duplication. Their partner has only one seat, directly opposite. A specified member of the second couple has four seats to choose from; their partner must then occupy the opposite seat. A specified member of the last couple has two choices, and their partner takes the remaining opposite seat.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N_B&=1\\times1\\times4\\times1\\times2\\times1\\\\N_B&=8\\\\N_B&=2^3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe opposite partners have no independent choices, so there is no additional factor of 2.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
